//compile_error: the Type metaclass is not a type argument. The manual
//closes the type-argument domain (§4.12.5: scalar primitive, string,
//enumeration, class, interface, struct, array, or another generic
//instantiation), and `Type` belongs to none of them. It has no keyword,
//and the runtime's builtin-type mirror gives up the internal name the
//runtime tables stringize for it, so the name resolves nowhere. This
//shape used to compile and then poison the image: the producer spelled
//the leaf "?" and the VM refused the module at start-up as a corrupt
//descriptor.
import io;

int main() {
    List<Type> l = List<Type>();
    io.print(l.length());
    return 0;
}
